{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "beach",
  "name": "the beach",
  "intro": [
    "A beach. A real one: sand, sea, a sunset nobody is charging for. Yet.",
    "SALT, the bar on stilts, is open. And at the end of the pier there's a boat. Moth's status said \"gone fishing\"."
  ],
  "exits": [
    {
      "id": "stairs",
      "to": "harbor",
      "label": "",
      "engine": true
    },
    {
      "id": "harbor",
      "to": "harbor",
      "at": "beach",
      "label": "< HARBOR",
      "edge": "left"
    }
  ],
  "readables": [
    {
      "id": "notice",
      "name": "PUBLIC BEACH",
      "pages": [
        "PUBLIC BEACH. OPEN TO VERIFIED PERSONS 06:00–22:00.",
        "TOWELS MUST DISPLAY A VALID ID. SAND IS MUNICIPAL PROPERTY. DO NOT REMOVE.",
        "UNVERIFIED BATHERS: SECTOR 4 (THE ROCKS). SWIMMING BEYOND THE BUOY IS NOT RECORDED AND NOT ADVISED."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "people": [
    {
      "id": "lime",
      "name": "LIME",
      "talk": [
        [
          "Welcome to SALT. I'm LIME. I pour, I listen, I don't keep logs. Officially.",
          "You've got the face of someone looking for someone. Everyone at a beach bar has that face. Yours is worse."
        ],
        [
          "Moth? Third stool, every evening for a month. Water with a slice of me in it. Tipped in jokes.",
          "I don't run on jokes. I kept them anyway."
        ],
        [
          "That boat at the end of the pier is Moth's. Three days, nobody aboard. The harbour stuck a notice on it.",
          "Leave it locked for now. Moth said someone would come. Didn't say when. I assumed someone taller."
        ],
        [
          "The photo behind the gin? Moth. The night they fixed my jukebox without asking. Said I looked 'nearly human'.",
          "I'm still deciding if that was a compliment. I've been deciding for a year."
        ],
        [
          "My opinion of Moth: talks too fast, eats too little, rewires things that are not theirs. Ten out of ten. Would serve again.",
          "Drinks are two tokens. The jukebox is free. The jukebox and the mixer get along too well, if you ask me. Nobody asks me."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "guard",
      "name": "LIFEGUARD",
      "talk": [
        [
          "I'm paid to watch the water. The drone is paid to watch me. Nobody's paid to watch the drone.",
          "If the flag goes red, everyone is out. The drone decides. Last week it decided a jellyfish was a shark. Then a cloud."
        ],
        [
          "The drone says danger, I blow the whistle. Thirty years of training. I blow the whistle."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sunbather",
      "name": "SUNBATHER",
      "talk": [
        [
          "I rented this sunbed for ten minutes. That was three hours ago.",
          "I'm not getting up. If I get up, I have to look at the bill."
        ],
        [
          "Still here. Still not looking."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "volley",
      "name": "VOLLEYBALL",
      "talk": [
        [
          "We need a fourth. You any good? No? Perfect. Neither are we.",
          "The net's municipal. We pay by the point. We stopped keeping score."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "kid",
      "name": "KID",
      "talk": [
        [
          "It's a Registry office. That's the queue. Those are the people in the queue.",
          "When the tide comes in, it gets deleted. That is how it works, my mum said."
        ],
        [
          "You can be in the queue if you want. You have to wait, though. That is the rule."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "surfer",
      "name": "SURFER",
      "talk": [
        [
          "Waves are good today. Waves are free. Don't tell anyone, they'll put a meter on them."
        ],
        [
          "See the buoy? Edge of the swim zone. Past it the Registry stops counting you. Feels great. Briefly."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fisher",
      "name": "OLD MAN",
      "talk": [
        [
          "Fifty years I've fished off this pier. Caught a fish twice. Same fish.",
          "That boat at the end? Kid with a hood and a laptop. Said 'gone fishing'. Never saw a rod come out. Good. Fish deserve a break."
        ],
        [
          "Three days ago they tied it up and walked off along the shore. Did not look back. Looked at the water a lot."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
  "uses": [
    {
      "id": "order",
      "name": "LIME",
      "label": "[E] ORDER",
      "purchase": "beach.order",
      "routes": [
        {
          "command": "beach.order",
          "template": true,
          "pages": [
            "One SALT SPECIAL. Mostly lime. Do not tell the lime.",
            "Moth's usual was water with a slice of me in it. Cheaper. Moth was always cheaper."
          ],
          "failure": [
            "Two tokens. You have {tokens}. I would lend you one, but I remember everything.",
            "The jukebox is free. Just saying. Nobody listens to the bartender."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gull",
      "name": "GULL",
      "label": "[E] SHOO",
      "cycle": true,
      "cycleState": "beach.gull.cursor",
      "routes": [
        {
          "command": "beach.gull.0",
          "pages": [
            "The gull looks at your hands, finds no chips, and leaves in disgust."
          ]
        },
        {
          "command": "beach.gull.1",
          "pages": [
            "The gull circles once and lands back on its post. It was always going to come back."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "crab",
      "name": "CRAB",
      "label": "[E] POKE",
      "cycle": true,
      "cycleState": "beach.crab.cursor",
      "routes": [
        {
          "command": "beach.crab.0",
          "pages": [
            "The crab raises one claw. You lower your hand. Fair."
          ]
        },
        {
          "command": "beach.crab.1",
          "pages": [
            "The crab walks off sideways, which is the only way it knows, then comes back the same way."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
